# CQ-24  Which activities (forecasting, planning, optimisation) is actor X
#        currently performing?
# Group F -- SHIFT is EXPECTED TO FAIL this.
#
# Parameters (method note 5): the actor of interest.
#
# MISSING TERM. SHIFT has no activity reification. It declares outputs and
# artefacts (shift:ForecastData, shift:FlexibilitySchedule) and participation
# links (shift:participatesIn, shift:participatesInFlexibility,
# shift:participatesInMarket), but:
#   - there is no Activity class, and none of ForecastingActivity /
#     PlanningActivity / OptimizationActivity exists;
#   - there is no performs / executes property from an Actor to an activity,
#     so "who is doing what, now" cannot be stated;
#   - the forecast artefact carries no agent, so even the producer of a
#     ForecastData individual is unrecoverable.
# The nearest SEAS equivalents are seas:Activity with its subclasses
# seas:ForecastingActivity, seas:PlanningActivity, seas:OptimizationActivity,
# and the seas:ActorOntology role/activity linkage. This is the CQ the paper
# expects SEAS to win.
#
# The query below is the closest SHIFT admits and returns nothing.
PREFIX shift: <https://w3id.org/shift/core#>
PREFIX xsd:   <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#>
SELECT ?actor ?activity
WHERE {
  # -- parameters --------------------------------------------------------
  VALUES ?ACTOR { <https://w3id.org/shift/kg/actor/A000> }
  # ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  BIND(?ACTOR AS ?actor)
  ?ACTOR shift:participatesIn ?activity .
}
ORDER BY ?activity
